RESULT {"run": "v1-int-e88f0806-r1", "case": "gobwas-ws-a567dfd6", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "outcome": "finished", "model_calls": 9, "tool_calls": 9, "in_tok": 20, "cache_write": 23172, "cache_read": 44580, "out_tok": 4148, "model_s": 37.18, "tool_s": 613.2, "commands": [{"cmd": "cd wsflate && grep -rn \"unexpected stream tail\" . ; git log --oneline | head -3; git status --short", "rc": 0, "s": 0.35}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && sed -n 1,160p writer.go; grep -n \"tail\\|Tail\" *.go | grep -v _test", "rc": 0, "s": 0.15}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && cat cbuf.go", "rc": 0, "s": 0.12}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && git diff HEAD --stat; ls", "rc": 0, "s": 0.22}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && cat helper.go; sed -n 1,50p writer_test.go; go test . 2>&1 | head -5", "rc": 127, "s": 0.2}, {"cmd": "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin:~/go/bin; which go; cd wsflate; grep -n \"Close\\|Flush\" *_test.go ../tests/deflate_test.go | head -30", "rc": 0, "s": 0.11}, {"cmd": "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; cd wsflate; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('writer.go').read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"\t\tw.err = c.Close()\n\t}\n\tw.checkTail()\n\"\"\",\"\"\"\t\tw.err = c.Close()\n\t}\n\"\"\")\nopen('writer.go','w').write(s)\nE\ncd ..; go test -count=1 github.com/gobwas/ws/tests github.com/gobwas/ws/wsflate 2>&1 | tail -20", "rc": 124, "s": 600.12}, {"cmd": "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; cd wsflate; timeout 60 go test -count=1 -timeout 20s . 2>&1 | head -30; cat reader.go | sed -n 1,120p", "rc": 0, "s": 5.03}, {"cmd": "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; cd wsflate; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('writer.go').read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"\tif c, ok := w.c.(io.Closer); ok {\n\t\tw.err = c.Close()\n\t}\n\"\"\",\"\"\"\t// The stream must already be terminated by a flushed tail. Closing a\n\t// compressor emits a final block, which is not allowed by PMCE, so verify\n\t// the tail first and discard whatever the compressor writes on Close().\n\tw.chec", "rc": 0, "s": 6.91}], "final_text": "The tests in `tests` and `wsflate` now pass (`go test -count=1 github.com/gobwas/ws/tests github.com/gobwas/ws/wsflate`).\n\n**Cause:** `wsflate.Writer.Close()` called `Close()` on the underlying `compress/flate` writer. That emits a final empty block (`03 00`) after the sync-flush tail (`00 00 ff ff`). The writer's tail buffer (`cbuf`) holds back the last 4 bytes, so the stream then ended in `ff ff 03 00`. `checkTail()` rejected that with \"unexpected stream tail\".\n\nTaking out the tail check alone isn't enough. The extra bytes corrupt the permessage-deflate payload, and the decompressor fails with \"corrupt input\".\n\n**Fix (in `wsflate/writer.go`):** `Close()` now does three things:\n1. It runs `checkTail()` first, while the flushed tail is still intact.\n2. It points the tail buffer's destination at `ioutil.Discard`.\n3. It then closes the compressor, so the final block it writes goes nowhere and the payload stays valid.\n\nOne behaviour to be aware of: calling `Close()` without a prior `Flush()` still returns the bad-tail error, as it did before.", "patch": "diff --git a/wsflate/writer.go b/wsflate/writer.go\nindex 0342ccb..0d929a6 100644\n--- a/wsflate/writer.go\n+++ b/wsflate/writer.go\n@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ package wsflate\n import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"io\"\n+\t\"io/ioutil\"\n )\n \n var (\n@@ -104,13 +105,20 @@ func (w *Writer) Flush() error {\n // Close closes Writer and a Compressor instance used under the hood (if it\n // implements io.Closer interface).\n func (w *Writer) Close() error {\n+\tif w.err != nil {\n+\t\treturn w.err\n+\t}\n+\t// The stream must already be terminated by a flushed tail. Closing a\n+\t// compressor emits a final block, which is not allowed by PMCE, so verify\n+\t// the tail first and discard whatever the compressor writes on Close().\n+\tw.checkTail()\n \tif w.err != nil {\n \t\treturn w.err\n \t}\n \tif c, ok := w.c.(io.Closer); ok {\n+\t\tw.cbuf.dst = ioutil.Discard\n \t\tw.err = c.Close()\n \t}\n-\tw.checkTail()\n \treturn w.err\n }\n \n", "total_s": 652.03}
